WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.414 --> 00:00:03.250
(inspirational music)

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.170
- We are creating the world's largest

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:09.200
acrylic mural by a single artist.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.700
But I knew that I didn't
want to have just a mural.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.680
It had to be a project
that really dove deeper

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.820
into the needs in the
community, and what a perfect

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.250
opportunity to do it in these
massive grain elevators.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.840
My name is Armando Minjarez.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.813
And I'm the project director
and curator for Horizontes.

00:00:35.512 --> 00:00:38.512
(soft guitar music)

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.100
I immigrated to the United States in 2001.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.800
I am an artist, but I've also
been a community organizer

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.958
working on mostly immigrant rights.

00:00:48.958 --> 00:00:52.300
So, the work that I do now really combines

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.230
my work as a community organizer

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:57.300
and bringing that into creative expression

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.050
and kind of mixing those two.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.230
Horizontes, it's a large-scale

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:04.010
community engagement art project.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:04.910
There's another one that was painted

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:06.700
as part of the project, too.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.620
This is painted by
Heather, and these are all

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.408
women from the north
end, and these are all

00:01:10.408 --> 00:01:14.810
her (speaking foreign language).

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.690
The women from her family that grew up

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:17.770
in the neighborhood.

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.460
The project really focuses
on bringing solidarity

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.920
between the primarily Latino neighborhood

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.070
and the historically
African-American neighborhoods.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.160
With these murals, one
of my personal goals

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.460
is to have people of
color depicted in the most

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.363
magnificent way that we could.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.367
(inspirational music)

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.290
The people that are depicted in the mural

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.100
are people that used to
live in the neighborhood,

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.492
or they currently live
in the neighborhood.

00:01:48.492 --> 00:01:51.800
We went and dig through
the historical archives

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.000
and pulled photographs
from the people that helped

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.320
build the tracks that we're surrounded by.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.103
Those were Mexican laborers
that came 100 years ago.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.960
Thanks to the internet, I've found Gleo.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.372
She had painted some
giant towers in Brazil,

00:02:06.372 --> 00:02:08.810
so I knew that she had the skill

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.693
and the ability to paint large-scale.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.896
And she flew down from
Colombia into Kansas,

00:02:13.896 --> 00:02:16.623
and she's been here
working on the project.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.922
- [Armando] What I hope that
this means to the community

00:02:54.922 --> 00:02:58.400
is that we feel proud
of where we come from,

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.170
that we take ownership
of our neighborhoods,

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:05.360
of our communities, and
continue to expand this work.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.100
All of us hold different identities.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.990
We're people of color, we're immigrants,

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.000
we're queer people, women.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.010
Here we are painting the
world's largest mural,

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.810
not because we want to hold the record,

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:18.247
but because it's our
stories that need to be told

00:03:18.247 --> 00:03:20.880
and to remind ourselves
that we need to continue

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:21.963
to work together.

